    793  029d							; Gravity spin direction now follows Major Tom's actual approach
    794  029d							; velocity, not just his static side of the beacon. Sign of the
    795  029d							; angular-momentum cross product L = relX*velY - relY*velX gives the
    796  029d							; physically-continuous spin direction (screen Y increases downward,
    797  029d							; so positive L is clockwise here rather than the usual math
    798  029d							; convention). relX/relY are Tom's center relative to the beacon
